scimesh Changes
===============

Version 0.4.0 -- Batch primitives, tubes, line layers and text labels
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- BRK: clip planes are defined in **world space** by default.  In 0.3.4 and
  earlier `normal`/`offset` were interpreted in eye (camera) space, so the cut
  travelled with the camera and had to be re-tuned for every viewpoint.  Pass
  `clip_plane(..., space = "eye")` (R) or `PlaneSpace::EYE` (C++) for the old
  behaviour.
- BRK: fog distances (`fog_start`/`fog_end`) are now **world units** (distance
  from the camera), i.e. independent of the near/far planes and of the
  projection type.  `fog_space = "ndc"` (R) / `FogSpace::NDC` (C++) restores the
  old interpretation as raw depth buffer values.
- NEW: polyline tubes.  `generate_tube()` sweeps a circular cross-section along a
  path of points, `generate_multi_tubes()` batches many paths into one mesh.  The
  cross-section frames use parallel transport, so tubes do not twist around their
  own axis, and the mitered joints are watertight.  R: `generate_tube()`,
  `generate_tubes()`.
- NEW: spline sampling (`src/core/scimesh/spline.h`, header-only) turns a coarse
  list of 3D waypoints into a dense smooth path.  C++: `catmull_rom_path()`,
  `hermite_path()`, `bspline_path()`, `bezier_path()`, `resample_by_arclength()`,
  `path_length()`, `path_tangents()`, `path_curvature()`.  R: `spline_path()`,
  `bezier_path()`, `resample_path()`, `path_length()`, `path_curvature()` (see
  `examples/cpp/spline_tube/` and `examples/R/spline_tube/`).
- NEW: line layers — lines as scene primitives, with a width **in pixels** and
  without geometry, for wireframes, graph or connectome edges and trajectories.
  They are drawn together with the meshes (same camera, same depth buffer,
  back-to-front blending) and count towards the scene bounding box unless
  `affects_bounds = FALSE`, so decoration (a scale bar, an axis cross) can never
  push the camera away from the data.  R: `line_layer()`, `scene(lines = )`,
  `render_segments()`, `scene_set_line_affects_bounds()`; C++:
  `Renderer::render_lines_raw()`.
- NEW: R `camera_fit_scene()` fits a camera to a whole scene (meshes plus the
  line layers), the scene counterpart of the mesh-only `camera_auto()`.
- NEW: the batched primitive generators (one mesh for thousands of spheres or
  cylinders) are now available in R: `generate_multi_spheres()`,
  `generate_multi_cylinders()`, `generate_multi_tubes()`.  `generate_cylinder()`
  and `generate_multi_cylinders()` gained a `caps` argument.
- FIX: the C++ core now compiles with libc++ (macOS), which fixes the
  installation ERROR reported by the CRAN checks for 0.3.4 on the macOS flavors
  (`primitives.cpp` used `std::array`/`std::swap` without their includes, which
  libstdc++ pulls in transitively).
- NEW: global anti-aliasing default.  `render_options(aa_samples = NULL)` (the
  new default) resolves from the global option `scimesh.aa_samples`, so
  `options(scimesh.aa_samples = 2)` anti-aliases every render call that does not
  pass `aa_samples` explicitly.
- NEW: text labels — `TextLayer` annotations without any geometry, drawn on top
  of the meshes and lines.  Positions are world space (the label sticks to the
  annotated location and is hidden by geometry in front of it unless
  `depth_test = FALSE`) or screen space (titles, panel tags), the font size is in
  pixels, and `adj`, pixel offsets, rotation and halos are supported.  R:
  `text_layer()`, `scene(texts = )`, `render_text()`, `text_extent()`,
  `world_to_screen()`.  C++: `Font`, `draw_text()`, `measure_text()`.  The bundled
  Inter font can be replaced with `SCIMESH_FONT`, and `full_CLI_renderer` gained
  the `--text*` options and a `[text]` config section.
- NEW: `flip_uvs()` (C++ and R) mirrors the `v` texture coordinate of a mesh,
  the documented conversion for UVs that use the bottom-left origin (OBJ, PLY,
  rgl, OpenGL, Blender).  scimesh UVs are image space (`v = 0` = top row).
- NEW: R `clip_plane()` creates and validates clip plane descriptors, and
  `render_options()` validates `clip_planes` and the fog settings and exposes the
  `near_plane`/`far_plane` options (defaults 0.1 and 10000, matching C++).
- NEW: `full_CLI_renderer` example: `[fog] space` config key and `--fog-space`
  flag, and `--output brain.png` no longer writes `brain.png.png`.
- DEP: vendored libfs updated to commit ab88cb4 (v0.6.1 plus the `inline` fix),
  which unbreaks linking for consumers that include `libfs.h` in more than one
  translation unit.  scimesh only reads meshes through libfs.
- FIX: `scale_mesh()`, `rotate_mesh()` and `transform_mesh()` now update
  per-vertex normals (inverse transpose, renormalized), so shading is correct
  after scaling, rotation, shear or mirroring.
- FIX: `mesh_from_fs(detect_transparency = TRUE)` could never mark anything as
  transparent, so FreeSurfer medial walls were rendered opaque white.  NaN
  vertices (FreeSurfer's "no data" marker) are now transparent, and C++
  `convert_fs_mesh(..., nan_alpha = )` can give them any alpha.
- FIX: screen-space ambient occlusion (`ssao_enabled = TRUE`) had no visible
  effect at all: the depth buffer was linearized with the wrong range,
  `ssao_radius` was used as a world factor instead of pixels, and the hemisphere
  test had the wrong sign.
- FIX: transparency.  Translucent geometry behind opaque geometry was blended on
  top of it (the blended pass ignored the depth test), and the translucent pass
  sorted front-to-back instead of back-to-front.  Transparency is now detected
  from the colors (`Mesh::is_transparent()`, no need to set
  `has_transparency`), PLY vertex alpha is kept instead of dropped, and R gained
  `set_mesh_alpha()`.
- FIX: rendering a double-sided mesh was platform dependent: coplanar front and
  back faces were decided by floating point rounding (an opaque plane could come
  out speckled with ambient-lit pixels), and a pixel center exactly on a shared
  triangle edge was covered twice or not at all (a seam on translucent planes).
  Back faces are now shaded two-sided and edge coverage follows a deterministic
  fill rule.
- DOC: `direction` in `camera_auto()`/`camera_fit_*()` was documented as the
  view direction, but it is the side the camera is placed on
  (`center + direction * distance`).  Mesh UVs are image space.
- DEV: C++ code coverage can be measured locally (`-DSCIMESH_COVERAGE=ON`,
  `dev_tools/coverage_cpp.sh`), and a new CI workflow builds and runs all C++ and
  R examples on every push/PR.

Version 0.3.4 -- Minor fix for CRAN only
-----------------------------------------
- FIX: adapt link in docs to prevent winbuilder warning


Version 0.3.3 -- Scene transforms, scene object, glTF export
------------------------------------------------------------
- NEW: per-mesh placement transforms in the C++ Scene.  A scene now stores an
  optional model matrix (and name) per mesh; the renderer applies it as a model
  transform at render time, so meshes are no longer modified in place.  See
  Scene::add(), Scene::set_transform(), Scene::node()/nodes() in scene.h.
  Scene::compute_bounding_box() now accounts for placement transforms.
- NEW: first-class scene object in the R layer: `scene()` builds an S3 object
  of class 'scimesh_scene' bundling meshes (each with an optional 4x4 placement
  transform and name), a camera, and render options.  `render_scene()` accepts
  it (and still accepts plain mesh lists as before).
- NEW: glTF 2.0 export, one-way interoperability: new C++ header gltf_io.h
  writes .gltf (+ external .bin) and self-contained .glb files with geometry,
  per-node transforms and names, vertex colors (COLOR_0), and an optional
  camera.  New R function `write_gltf()` wraps it.  Renderer-specific settings
  (fog, SSAO, shading mode) are not part of glTF and are not exported;
  per-face colors are exported by splitting vertices.
- CHG: `transform_mesh()` and the Rcpp matrix conversion now interpret 4x4
  matrices in the standard row-major convention (M * p, translation in the
  last column).  Previously the matrix was effectively applied transposed,
  which only diagonal (scaling) matrices hid; non-diagonal inputs now behave
  as written.  `scene()` placement transforms follow the same convention.
- CHG: `render_scene()`'s `camera` and `options` arguments are now optional
  and fall back to the values stored in a 'scimesh_scene' when present
  (backwards compatible).
- DOC: new R docs for scene(), write_gltf(); updated render_scene() docs.


Version 0.3.2 -- CRAN review fixes
-----------------------------------
- FIX: do not strip debug symbols for R build, as per CRAN policy
- FIX: add more input checks and disable use of asserts in third-party code, as per CRAN policy that C++ code should not call assert
- NEW: full_CLI_renderer example: composite mode now supports --crop/--grow to pre-process each tile (e.g. trim colorbar whitespace) before arranging
- NEW: full_CLI_renderer example: add --info mode to print image dimensions ('<path> WxH') without external tools like ImageMagick's identify
- NEW: add composite_tight.sh example that produces compact, publication-style multi-view figures: crop each rendered view (--crop --grow), arrange via --composite --fit-mode pad (auto max-extent padding, no manual image sizing), then attach a trimmed colorbar


Version 0.3.1 -- TGA support, macOS fix
----------------------------------------
- FIX: make R package compile again unter MacOS by avoiding strip --strip-debug in Makevars, the MacOS version of strip does not support --strip-debug.
- NEW: add TGA image export (own uncompressed true-color writer, no dependencies) to the C++ layer and the R layer via new `write_tga()` function (32-bit RGBA default, optional 24-bit RGB)
- improve all c++ doc strings for better API docs
- DEP: update libfs to commit 2641453 which fixes version define typo
- CHG: default to white instead of transparent background
- DOC: add cpp example that is a full command line program that renders meshes
- DOC: add file in source tree that lists all third-party details with full licenses, see src/third_party/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (and a copy for R at LICENSE.note)


Version 0.3.0 -- Dependencies, repo structure, C++ versioning
------------------------------------------------------------
- BRK: move scimesh code from src/core/ to src/core/scimesh and all required downstream adjustments. avoids conflicts with other libraries in C++ layer
- NEW: get proper versioning in place for C++ layer
- SEC: Update libfs to v0.4.1
- DOC: dramatically improve all doc strings, integrate CPP_GETTING_STARTED into API docs
- NEW: add colorbar application functions (C++ and R)


